From 86e8baefb9e6e149ada87efb618414f4eb4b00a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P4R4D16M4 <patrickheinzelbecker@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:42:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] comcerto-nand: accept the ECC state a previous kernel
 leaves after kexec

The system kernel is started by kexec from the UntrashOS loader, which
has already read the NAND.  The ECC engine is then in the read state
this driver leaves after a clean read (gen=0x00080400, CS4, idle,
poly=0), not in the Barebox write/generate state the probe required.
The probe refused with -EUCLEAN, so the system kernel had no NAND:
/proc/mtd was empty and untrash-pfe-firmware could not copy the stock
PFE firmware from rootfs1 (r24 on hardware: no network, fallback to A).

Accept exactly that state as well.  Every read step still sets read
mode itself; the MTD stays read-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
index 5ea4f5c..a437b66 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
@@ -1359,6 +1359,20 @@ static int comcerto_nand_validate_stock_ecc_state(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	u32 idle = readl(cn->ecc + COMCERTO_ECC_IDLE_STAT);
 	u32 poly = readl(cn->ecc + COMCERTO_ECC_POLY_STAT);
 
+	/*
+	 * After kexec from the UntrashOS loader the controller is in the state
+	 * this driver leaves after a clean read (read mode, CS4, idle, no
+	 * correction pending), not in the Barebox write/generate state.
+	 */
+	if (gen == COMCERTO_ECC_GEN_READ_1BIT_1024 &&
+	    cs == COMCERTO_ECC_CS4_SELECTED &&
+	    (idle & COMCERTO_ECC_IDLE) && !(poly & BIT(0))) {
+		dev_notice(&pdev->dev,
+			   "inherited ECC state of a previous kernel verified (read mode, CS4, idle, poly=%08x)\n",
+			   poly);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (gen != COMCERTO_ECC_GEN_WRITE_1BIT_1024 ||
 	    cs != COMCERTO_ECC_CS4_SELECTED ||
 	    !(idle & COMCERTO_ECC_IDLE) ||
